				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1291,
				7
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement AES-256-GCM secure IPC channel with key rotation\n\nIntroduce the `SecureMessageChannel` module within the Mountain backend's IPC layer to provide end-to-end encryption and integrity verification for all native-to-extension and native-to-ui communications.\n\nThe implementation establishes a tightly-coupled cluster of Rust structs adhering to PascalCase naming:\n- `Channel::Struct`: The core aggregator managing AES-256-GCM encryption, HMAC-SHA256 signing, and automatic key rotation via Tokio background tasks.\n- `EncryptionKey::Struct`: Wraps `ring` key material with metadata (ID, creation time, usage count) to support seamless rotation.\n- `EncryptedMessage::Struct` & `SecureMessage::Struct<T>`: DTOs for the encrypted envelope and the generic secure message wrapper with routing headers.\n- `SecurityConfig::Struct` & `SecurityStats::Struct`: Configuration for rotation intervals and runtime telemetry for key age and usage.\n\nKey security features include:\n- **Automatic Key Rotation**: Periodic generation of new encryption keys while retaining previous keys for a defined window to allow in-flight message decryption.\n- **Replay Protection**: Timestamp validation to reject messages older than 5 minutes.\n- **Integrity Verification**: HMAC-SHA256 signatures on all ciphertext to prevent tampering.\n- **DOs Mitigation**: Configurable maximum message size limits.\n\nThis module upgrades the IPC architecture from implicit trust to cryptographically secure communication, aligning with the `ValidatePermission` engine and the distributed architecture's security requirements.",
			"SHA": "01058e0646a63733f48928c2f2d744dac41fd4af"
		}
	],
